IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg11-s388-domestication`
IMPORT `dg11-s389-temporary-transfer`
IMPORT `dg11-s390-transfer-out`
IMPORT `dg11-s391-fees`
IMPORT `dg11-s393-s398-miscellaneous`
IMPORT `dg11-s395-trust-in-name`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 (sections 101 to 398), Subchapter XVII (sections 388 to 390) and Subchapter XVIII (sections 391 to 398) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- LAYER 2. Nothing here is new law: every question calls a rule of the layer-1 modules imported above and restates none of them.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation Law (an incorporator, a director or officer, a stockholder
-- including a minority stockholder), asking what the Law lets them do, what it requires of them, what they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them.
-- The Secretary of State, the Court of Chancery and the Attorney General get no seat: their acts appear only as what they mean for the person (what the person is owed by them, or must give them).
--
-- THE FACTS ASKED. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates, and the modules' own short lists of choices -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc
-- worded as the person would be asked. The records the layer-1 rules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called.
-- Where a rule's answer can be "the text does not say" (a MAYBE with NOTHING), the question's answer can be too; a question that answers NOTHING means the text of the Law does not settle that case.
-- A date or a fact that applies only if something else is true (for example "the date it was filed, if it has been") is asked as a yes/no question and a date; the date is ignored when the answer is no.
-- Judgments the Law leaves to someone else (the Secretary of State's waiver, the directors' determination under section 389(i), the officials' determination under section 395(d)(3), the management's
-- judgment under section 389(c)(4)f.) are asked as facts the person states -- "has the Secretary of State waived ...?" -- and never guessed.
--
-- GROUPS. The § headings below follow the Law's order. A group that arises only in a situation the person may not be in says so in its comment, so that a form can ask "has this happened to you?" first:
--   Section 388 -- your non-United States entity is becoming a Delaware corporation by domestication.
--   Section 389 -- your non-United States entity is moving its domicile into Delaware because of an emergency condition.
--   Section 390 -- your Delaware corporation is moving out of Delaware (transfer, domestication or continuance in a foreign jurisdiction).
--   Section 391 -- you are filing something with the Secretary of State, or have been asked to pay a fee.
--   Sections 393 to 398 -- general.
--
-- Where this layer departs from the defaults (recorded, not fixed): section 391 states some fees only as a ceiling ("up to $175"); the Secretary of State's schedule is not among the inputs, so those
-- questions answer "the most I can be charged". The sums that other provisions fix for a filing (the county and courthouse assessments of section 103(c)(6) and (7), in piece dg1) are not part of these answers.

§ `Choices used by the questions`

-- The kinds of entity a person can name for a non-United States entity. The core's `Kind of entity` has a constructor that carries a field (`a corporation` carries the Kind of corporation under this chapter),
-- which cannot be a plain choice; this list is the plain choice, and the question's WHERE turns it into the core's value.
DECLARE `dg11 seat Kind of foreign entity` IS ONE OF
    `an entity that is a corporation`
    `an entity that is a limited liability company`
    `an entity that is a statutory trust`
    `an entity that is a business trust or association`
    `an entity that is a real estate investment trust`
    `an entity that is a common-law trust`
    `an entity that is a general partnership`
    `an entity that is a limited partnership`
    `an entity that is a limited liability partnership`
    `an entity that is a limited liability limited partnership`
    `an entity that is a joint-stock association`
    `an entity that is any other unincorporated business or association`
    `a natural person, who is not an entity`

-- Placeholder: for `a corporation`, the core's field `its kind` says which Kind of corporation under THIS chapter (section 114(d)); an entity formed abroad is not organized under this chapter, so the field has no
-- meaning here and no rule of these modules reads it. It is given the fixed value `a stock corporation`.
GIVEN kind IS A `dg11 seat Kind of foreign entity`
GIVETH A `Kind of entity`
`dg11 seat the core's kind of entity for` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an entity that is a corporation` THEN `a corporation` WITH `its kind` IS `a stock corporation`
    WHEN `an entity that is a limited liability company` THEN `a limited liability company`
    WHEN `an entity that is a statutory trust` THEN `a statutory trust`
    WHEN `an entity that is a business trust or association` THEN `a business trust or association`
    WHEN `an entity that is a real estate investment trust` THEN `a real estate investment trust`
    WHEN `an entity that is a common-law trust` THEN `a common-law trust`
    WHEN `an entity that is a general partnership` THEN `a general partnership`
    WHEN `an entity that is a limited partnership` THEN `a limited partnership`
    WHEN `an entity that is a limited liability partnership` THEN `a limited liability partnership`
    WHEN `an entity that is a limited liability limited partnership` THEN `a limited liability limited partnership`
    WHEN `an entity that is a joint-stock association` THEN `a joint-stock association`
    WHEN `an entity that is any other unincorporated business or association` THEN `any other unincorporated business or association`
    WHEN `a natural person, who is not an entity` THEN `a natural person`

§ `Section 388 - becoming a Delaware corporation by domestication`

-- SITUATION: your non-United States entity (an entity formed under the laws of a foreign jurisdiction) is becoming, or has become, a Delaware corporation by domestication.

§§ `388(a) to (h) - the filing, the signature, the approval and the certificate`

-- s 388(a)(2), (b), (h). The entity's power to become a Delaware corporation: by complying with subsection (h) and filing a certificate of corporate domestication and a certificate of incorporation, together.
@export May my non-United States entity become domesticated as a corporation in Delaware (s 388(a)(2), (b), (h))?
GIVEN `my entity is of this kind` IS A `dg11 seat Kind of foreign entity` @desc What kind of entity is it?
      `my entity was formed under the laws of` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Where was your entity first formed, incorporated or created?
      `its governing document or applicable non-United States law provides for the approval and the domestication has been approved that way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the domestication been approved in the manner that the entity's governing document, or applicable non-United States law, provides?
      `that approval was given before the certificate of corporate domestication became effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that approval given before the certificate of corporate domestication became effective?
      `the certificate of incorporation was approved by the same authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of incorporation approved by the same authorization that approved the domestication?
      `the certificate of corporate domestication was signed by an authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of corporate domestication signed by a person authorized to sign it for the entity?
      `the certificate of corporate domestication was filed in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of corporate domestication filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 103?
      `the certificate of incorporation was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of incorporation executed, acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with section 103?
      `the two certificates were filed at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the two certificates filed with the Secretary of State at the same time?
      `the certificates become effective upon their filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the certificates to become effective upon their filing?
      `each certificate provides for the same later effective date or time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If they are not to become effective upon filing, does each certificate provide for the same effective date or time in accordance with section 103(d)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(b) May my entity become domesticated as a Delaware corporation` IF
    `s 388(b) the non-United States entity may become domesticated as a corporation in this State`
        (`dg11 seat the core's kind of entity for` `my entity is of this kind`)
        `my entity was formed under the laws of`
        (`s 388(h) the domestication has been approved as required`
            `its governing document or applicable non-United States law provides for the approval and the domestication has been approved that way`
            `that approval was given before the certificate of corporate domestication became effective`
            `the certificate of incorporation was approved by the same authorization`)
        filing
    WHERE
        filing MEANS `s 388(b) Filing with the Secretary of State` WITH
            `certificate of corporate domestication executed in accordance with subsection (g)` IS `the certificate of corporate domestication was signed by an authorized person`
            `certificate of corporate domestication filed in accordance with § 103` IS `the certificate of corporate domestication was filed in accordance with section 103`
            `certificate of incorporation executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with § 103` IS `the certificate of incorporation was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103`
            `the two certificates are filed simultaneously with the Secretary of State` IS `the two certificates were filed at the same time`
            `the certificates are to become effective upon their filing, as § 103(d) permits` IS `the certificates become effective upon their filing`
            `each certificate provides for the same effective date or time in accordance with § 103(d)` IS `each certificate provides for the same later effective date or time`

-- s 388(a)(2). Is the entity a "non-United States entity" at all?
@export Is my entity a non-United States entity within the meaning of section 388(a)(2)?
GIVEN `my entity is of this kind` IS A `dg11 seat Kind of foreign entity` @desc What kind of entity is it?
      `my entity was formed under the laws of` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Where was your entity first formed, incorporated or created?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(a)(2) Is my entity a non-United States entity` IF
    `s 388(a)(2) the entity is a non-United States entity` (`dg11 seat the core's kind of entity for` `my entity is of this kind`) `my entity was formed under the laws of`

-- s 388(g). The signature: the person's power, and nobody else's, to sign for the entity.
@export May I sign the certificate of corporate domestication for my entity (s 388(g))?
GIVEN `I am authorized to sign the certificate of corporate domestication on behalf of my entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you authorized to sign the certificate of corporate domestication on behalf of the non-United States entity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(g) May I sign the certificate of corporate domestication` IF
    `s 388(g) the person may sign the certificate of corporate domestication` `I am authorized to sign the certificate of corporate domestication on behalf of my entity`

-- s 388(h). The approval, by itself.
@export Has the domestication of my entity been approved as section 388(h) requires?
GIVEN `it has been approved in the manner provided by the governing document or applicable non-United States law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the domestication been approved in the manner that the entity's governing document, or applicable non-United States law, provides?
      `it was approved before the certificate of corporate domestication became effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that approval given before the certificate of corporate domestication became effective in accordance with section 103?
      `the certificate of incorporation was approved by the same authorization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of incorporation approved by the same authorization that approved the domestication?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(h) Has the domestication of my entity been approved as required` IF
    `s 388(h) the domestication has been approved as required`
        `it has been approved in the manner provided by the governing document or applicable non-United States law`
        `it was approved before the certificate of corporate domestication became effective`
        `the certificate of incorporation was approved by the same authorization`

-- s 388(c). The contents of the certificate of corporate domestication.
@export Does my certificate of corporate domestication say everything that section 388(c) requires?
GIVEN `it gives the date on which and jurisdiction where the entity was first formed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate give the date on which, and jurisdiction where, the entity was first formed, incorporated, created or otherwise came into being?
      `it gives the name of the entity immediately before the filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the name of the non-United States entity immediately before the filing of the certificate?
      `it gives the name of the corporation as in its certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the name of the corporation as set forth in its certificate of incorporation?
      `it gives the jurisdiction of the seat or principal place of business immediately before the filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the jurisdiction that was the seat, siege social, or principal place of business or central administration of the entity immediately before the filing?
      `it certifies that the domestication shall be approved before the certificate takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify that the domestication shall be approved before the certificate takes effect, in the manner provided for by the governing document or by applicable non-United States law?
      `it certifies that all provisions of the plan shall be approved before the certificate takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify that all provisions of the plan of domestication shall be approved before the certificate takes effect, in accordance with all applicable non-United States law? (Say no if there is no plan.)
      `a plan of domestication is adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a plan of domestication adopted under section 388(l)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(c) Does my certificate of corporate domestication say everything required` IF
    `s 388(c) the certificate of corporate domestication certifies everything that subsection (c) requires` certifies `a plan of domestication is adopted`
    WHERE
        certifies MEANS `s 388(c) What the certificate of corporate domestication certifies` WITH
            `date on which and jurisdiction where the non-United States entity was first formed, incorporated, created or otherwise came into being` IS `it gives the date on which and jurisdiction where the entity was first formed`
            `name of the non-United States entity immediately prior to the filing of the certificate` IS `it gives the name of the entity immediately before the filing`
            `name of the corporation as set forth in its certificate of incorporation` IS `it gives the name of the corporation as in its certificate of incorporation`
            `jurisdiction that constituted its seat, siege social, or principal place of business or central administration, immediately prior to the filing` IS `it gives the jurisdiction of the seat or principal place of business immediately before the filing`
            `that the domestication shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of the certificate in the manner provided for` IS `it certifies that the domestication shall be approved before the certificate takes effect`
            `that all provisions of the plan of domestication shall be approved prior to the effectiveness of the certificate` IS `it certifies that all provisions of the plan shall be approved before the certificate takes effect`

§§ `388(d) to (f) - when the domestication takes effect, and what it leaves alone`

-- s 388(d). Is the entity now a Delaware corporation, subject to this title?
@export Has my entity become a corporation of Delaware, subject to this title (s 388(d))?
GIVEN `the certificate of corporate domestication has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate of corporate domestication become effective in accordance with section 103?
      `the certificate of incorporation has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate of incorporation become effective in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(d) Has my entity become a Delaware corporation` IF
    `s 388(d) the non-United States entity is domesticated as a corporation in this State, and the corporation is subject to all of the provisions of this title` `the certificate of corporate domestication has become effective` `the certificate of incorporation has become effective`

-- s 388(d). From what date does the corporation's existence run?
@export From what date is my corporation's existence deemed to have commenced after domestication (s 388(d))?
GIVEN `my entity has become domesticated as a corporation in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your entity become domesticated as a corporation in Delaware, with both certificates effective?
      `the date my entity first came into being where it was first formed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your entity commence its existence in the jurisdiction where it was first formed, incorporated or created? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2015-03-15)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 388(d) From what date does my corporation's existence run` IS
    `s 388(d) the date on which the existence of the corporation is deemed to have commenced` `my entity has become domesticated as a corporation in Delaware` `the date my entity first came into being where it was first formed`

-- s 388(e). Obligations, liabilities and personal liability.
@export Does the domestication change what my entity owes, or my personal liability for it (s 388(e))?
GIVEN `the matter is` IS A `s 388(e) Matter that the domestication leaves unaffected` @desc What is in question: an obligation or liability of the entity incurred before its domestication, the personal liability of a person for it, or another matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(e) Does the domestication leave my obligation or liability alone` IS
    `s 388(e) the domestication leaves the matter unaffected` `the matter is`

-- s 388(f). Which law applies, and from when.
@export Which law applies to my entity at a given time after I file the certificate of corporate domestication (s 388(f))?
GIVEN `the time I ask about is at or after the effective time of the domestication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the time you ask about at or after the effective time of the domestication?
GIVETH A `s 388(f) Law that applies to the non-United States entity`
DECIDE `s 388(f) Which law applies to my entity` IS
    `s 388(f) the law that applies to the entity at the time in question` `the time I ask about is at or after the effective time of the domestication`

§§ `388(i), (j) - the corporation is the same entity`

-- s 388(i). The same entity.
@export Is the corporation the same entity as my non-United States entity after domestication (s 388(i))?
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the domestication become effective under section 388?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(i) Is the corporation the same entity as my entity` IS
    `s 388(i) the corporation is deemed to be the same entity as the domesticating non-United States entity, a continuation of its existence` `the domestication has become effective`

-- s 388(i). Who holds the entity's property and rights.
@export In whom do my entity's rights, property and causes of action remain vested after domestication (s 388(i))?
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the domestication become effective under section 388?
      `my entity still exists where it was first formed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the non-United States entity continue its existence in the foreign jurisdiction where it existed just before the domestication?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 388(i) Who holds or bears after the domestication`
DECIDE `s 388(i) In whom do my entity's rights and property remain vested` IS
    `s 388(i) in whom the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the non-United States entity remain vested` `the domestication has become effective` `my entity still exists where it was first formed`

-- s 388(i). Who bears the entity's debts. The creditor's side of the same relation: against whom may I enforce a debt owed to me?
@export To whom do my entity's debts, liabilities and duties remain attached after domestication, so that I can enforce them (s 388(i))?
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the domestication become effective under section 388?
      `my entity still exists where it was first formed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the non-United States entity continue its existence in the foreign jurisdiction where it existed just before the domestication?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 388(i) Who holds or bears after the domestication`
DECIDE `s 388(i) To whom do my entity's debts and liabilities remain attached` IS
    `s 388(i) to whom the debts, liabilities and duties of the non-United States entity remain attached, to be enforced as if incurred by it as the corporation` `the domestication has become effective` `my entity still exists where it was first formed`

-- s 388(i). Title to real property.
@export Is the title to real property that my entity holds impaired by the domestication (s 388(i))?
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the domestication become effective under section 388?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(i) Is my entity's title to real property impaired` IS
    `s 388(i) title to real property vested in the non-United States entity reverts or is impaired by reason of this title` `the domestication has become effective`

-- s 388(i). Creditors' rights and liens: the creditor's side.
@export Are my rights as a creditor, and my liens on my debtor's property, preserved after the debtor's domestication (s 388(i))?
GIVEN `the domestication has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the domestication become effective under section 388?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(i) Are my creditor's rights and liens preserved` IS
    `s 388(i) the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of the non-United States entity are preserved unimpaired` `the domestication has become effective`

-- s 388(i). Whether the vesting is a "transfer".
@export Does the domestication count as a transfer of my entity's rights, property and debts to the corporation (s 388(i))?
GIVEN `the vesting or attaching results from the domestication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the vesting of the rights and property, and the attaching of the debts, result from the domestication?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(i) Does the domestication count as a transfer` IS
    `s 388(i) the rights, privileges, powers, interests in property, debts, liabilities and duties are deemed to have been transferred to the corporation` `the vesting or attaching results from the domestication`

-- s 388(j). Winding up and dissolution.
@export Must my entity wind up its affairs because it is domesticated as a Delaware corporation (s 388(j))?
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it otherwise agreed (for example in the entity's governing document or an agreement) that the entity must wind up?
      `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does applicable non-United States law otherwise require the entity to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(j) Must my entity wind up` IS
    `s 388(j) the domestication requires the domesticating non-United States entity to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets` `it is otherwise agreed` `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires`

@export Is the domestication of my entity a dissolution of it (s 388(j))?
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it otherwise agreed that the domestication is a dissolution?
      `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does applicable non-United States law otherwise require that the domestication be treated as a dissolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(j) Is the domestication a dissolution of my entity` IS
    `s 388(j) the domestication is deemed to constitute a dissolution of the non-United States entity` `it is otherwise agreed` `applicable non-United States law otherwise requires`

@export Do my entity and the Delaware corporation count as a single entity if my entity keeps existing where it was formed (s 388(j))?
GIVEN `my entity continues to exist where it was formed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Following domestication, does the entity continue its existence in the foreign jurisdiction where it existed just before domestication?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(j) Do my entity and the corporation count as a single entity` IS
    `s 388(j) the corporation and the non-United States entity constitute a single entity` `my entity continues to exist where it was formed`

§§ `388(k) to (m) - my shares, the plan, and corporate actions in the plan`

-- s 388(k). The holder's side: what can be done to my shares or interests.
@export Can my shares, rights, securities or interests in the entity be exchanged, converted or cancelled in the domestication (s 388(k))?
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `s 388(k) Treatment of the shares, rights, securities or interests of the non-United States entity` @desc What would be done to them: exchanged or converted into cash, into property, into shares or securities of the corporation, into cash, property or shares of another corporation or entity, or cancelled?
      `it is in connection with a domestication under section 388` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this done in connection with a domestication under section 388?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(k) Can my shares or interests be so treated` IS
    `s 388(k) the shares, rights, securities or interests may be so treated` `the treatment` `it is in connection with a domestication under section 388`

-- s 388(l). The plan.
@export May the plan of domestication state a given thing (s 388(l))?
GIVEN `the statement` IS A `s 388(l) Statement that a plan of domestication may make` @desc What would the plan state?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(l) May the plan of domestication state it` IS
    `s 388(l) the plan of domestication may state it` `the statement`

@export May a term of the plan of domestication depend on facts outside the plan (s 388(l))?
GIVEN `the plan sets out clearly and expressly how those facts operate on its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those facts operate upon the terms of the plan?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(l) May a term of the plan depend on facts outside the plan` IF
    `s 388(l) a term of the plan of domestication may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of the plan` `the plan sets out clearly and expressly how those facts operate on its terms`

@export May a term of the plan of domestication depend on this kind of fact (s 388(l))?
GIVEN `the fact is` IS A `s 388(l) Kind of fact on which a term of the plan may depend` @desc What kind of fact: the occurrence of an event, a determination or action by a person or body (including the entity or the corporation), or another kind of fact?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(l) May a term of the plan depend on this kind of fact` IS
    `s 388(l) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` `the fact is`

@export May the corporation take a corporate action stated in the plan of domestication (s 388(l)(v))?
GIVEN `the action has been approved under all applicable non-United States law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporate action stated in the plan been approved in accordance with all applicable non-United States law, including any approval required for that type of action?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(l)(v) May the corporation take the action stated in the plan` IF
    `s 388(l)(v) the corporate action stated in the plan may be taken` `the action has been approved under all applicable non-United States law`

-- s 388(m). A corporate action in the plan: does it need the board or stockholders again?
@export Does a corporate action in an approved plan of domestication need any further action of the board, the stockholders or the members (s 388(m))?
GIVEN `the action is in a plan approved in the manner provided by subsection (l)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action set forth in a plan of domestication approved in the manner provided for by section 388(l)?
      `the action is within the power of a corporation under subchapter II` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action within the power of a corporation under subchapter II of this chapter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(m) Is the action deemed approved with no further action` IS
    `s 388(m) the action is deemed authorized, adopted and approved, and needs no further action of the board of directors, stockholders or members under this title` `the action is in a plan approved in the manner provided by subsection (l)` `the action is within the power of a corporation under subchapter II`

@export Must the certificate I file under another section say that no further action is required (s 388(m))?
GIVEN `the action requires the filing of a certificate under another section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporate action require the filing of a certificate under another section of this title?
      `my certificate states that in accordance with section 388 no action is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that, in accordance with section 388, no action by the board of directors, stockholders, members or otherwise required by the other section is required?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 388(m) Does my certificate carry the required statement` IF
    `s 388(m) the certificate meets the requirement of the last sentence of subsection (m)` `the action requires the filing of a certificate under another section` `my certificate states that in accordance with section 388 no action is required`

§ `Section 389 - moving a non-United States entity's domicile into Delaware in an emergency`

-- SITUATION: your non-United States entity is moving, or has moved, its domicile into Delaware because of an emergency condition where it is governed (war, revolution, expropriation and the like).

§§ `389(a), (b) - what an emergency condition is; who may transfer`

-- s 389(a)(1).
@export Is this event an emergency condition for the purposes of section 389 (s 389(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the event is` IS A `s 389(a)(1) Event` @desc Which event? Pick the item on the list of section 389(a)(1) that fits, or "another event that subsection (a)(1) does not list".
      `the law governing my entity's internal affairs permits it to transfer its domicile on account of the event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an event under item j. (such other event): does the law of the jurisdiction governing the internal affairs of the entity permit the entity to transfer its domicile on account of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(a)(1) Is this event an emergency condition` IS
    `s 389(a)(1) the event is an emergency condition` `the event is` `the law governing my entity's internal affairs permits it to transfer its domicile on account of the event`

-- s 389(a)(3).
@export Do I count as an officer or a director of the non-United States entity for the purposes of section 389 (s 389(a)(3))?
GIVEN `I am an officer or a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or a director of the entity?
      `I am a trustee, a manager or a partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a trustee, a manager or a partner of the entity?
      `I perform functions equivalent to those of an officer or a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you perform functions equivalent to those of an officer or a director, however you are named or described in any relevant instrument?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(a)(3) Do I count as an officer or a director` IF
    `s 389(a)(3) the person counts as an officer or a director for the purposes of this section` `I am an officer or a director` `I am a trustee, a manager or a partner` `I perform functions equivalent to those of an officer or a director`

-- s 389(b).
@export May my non-United States entity transfer its domicile into Delaware (s 389(a)(2), (b))?
GIVEN `my entity is of this kind` IS A `dg11 seat Kind of foreign entity` @desc What kind of entity is it?
      `my entity was formed under the laws of` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Where was your entity first formed, incorporated or created?
      `my entity has complied with section 389` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity complied with section 389 (submitted and had accepted the documents of subsection (c), filed the annual certificates, and made the written communication of subsection (e))?
      `the law governing my entity's internal affairs expressly prohibits the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law by which the internal affairs of the entity are governed expressly prohibit such a transfer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(b) May my entity transfer its domicile into Delaware` IF
    `s 389(b) the non-United States entity may transfer its domicile into this State`
        (`dg11 seat the core's kind of entity for` `my entity is of this kind`)
        `my entity was formed under the laws of`
        `my entity has complied with section 389`
        `the law governing my entity's internal affairs expressly prohibits the transfer`

@export Does moving this place count as transferring my entity's domicile for the purposes of section 389 (s 389(b))?
GIVEN `the place is` IS A `s 389(b) Place that the entity moves` @desc Which place: the domicile, the seat, the siege social, the principal place of business, the central administration, or another equivalent under applicable law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(b) Does moving this place count as moving my domicile` IS
    `s 389(b) the place is the domicile of the entity for the purposes of this section` `the place is`

§§ `389(c) - what my entity submits to the Secretary of State, and when`

@export Did my entity submit its documents to the Secretary of State in time (s 389(c))?
GIVEN `we submitted the documents on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the entity submit the documents of section 389(c) to the Secretary of State? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)
      `we propose to transfer our domicile on` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the transfer of domicile proposed? (ISO 8601)
      `the Secretary of State has waived the 30-day period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State waived the 30-day period on the entity's request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(c) Did my entity submit its documents in time` IF
    `s 389(c) the documents were submitted in time` `we submitted the documents on` `we propose to transfer our domicile on` `the Secretary of State has waived the 30-day period`

@export Do the documents my entity submitted satisfy the requirements of section 389 (s 389(c))?
GIVEN `we submitted a copy of our certificate of incorporation and bylaws, certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the entity submit a copy of its certificate of incorporation and bylaws (or the equivalent under applicable law), certified as true and correct by the appropriate director, officer or government official?
      `we submitted a certificate of our existence from the jurisdiction governing our internal affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it submit a certificate issued by an authorized official of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs evidencing its existence?
      `we submitted the list of our authorized officers and directors with their agreements on service of process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it submit a list of the persons who shall be its authorized officers and directors, with evidence of their authority and their executed agreements in writing regarding service of process?
      `we submitted the certificate executed by the appropriate officer or director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it submit the certificate executed by the appropriate officer or director described in section 389(c)(4)?
      `the examination fee we paid, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much examination fee did the entity pay, in dollars?
      `it names our registered agent in this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that certificate set forth the name and address of the entity's registered agent in this State?
      `it describes our business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth a general description of the business in which the entity is engaged?
      `it states that the filing was duly authorized and violates nothing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the filing has been duly authorized by any necessary action and does not violate the certificate of incorporation or bylaws or any material agreement or instrument binding on the entity?
      `it lists who may sign the written communications of subsection (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it list the persons authorized to sign the written communications required by section 389(e)?
      `it affirms that the transfer is not expressly prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it affirm that the transfer is not expressly prohibited under the law by which the entity's internal affairs are governed?
      `it undertakes that the transfer will be made only in an emergency condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it undertake that any transfer of domicile will take place only in the event of an emergency condition, and will continue only so long as the emergency condition, in the judgment of the entity's management, so requires?
      `any of the documents is not in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the documents not in English?
      `a translation under oath of the translator is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is a translation, under oath of the translator, attached?
      `the Secretary of State has waived the translation requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State waived the translation requirement on the entity's request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(c) Do my entity's documents satisfy section 389` IF
    `s 389(c) the documents satisfy the requirements of this section` submitted `sets forth`
        (`s 389(c) the translation requirement is met` `any of the documents is not in English` `a translation under oath of the translator is attached` `the Secretary of State has waived the translation requirement`)
    WHERE
        submitted MEANS `s 389(c) What the entity submitted` WITH
            `copy of its certificate of incorporation and bylaws, or the equivalent, certified as true and correct by the appropriate director, officer or government official` IS `we submitted a copy of our certificate of incorporation and bylaws, certified`
            `certificate issued by an authorized official of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs evidencing its existence` IS `we submitted a certificate of our existence from the jurisdiction governing our internal affairs`
            `list of the persons who shall be its authorized officers and directors, with evidence of their authority and their executed agreements regarding service of process` IS `we submitted the list of our authorized officers and directors with their agreements on service of process`
            `certificate executed by the appropriate officer or director` IS `we submitted the certificate executed by the appropriate officer or director`
            `examination fee prescribed under § 391` IS `the examination fee we paid, in dollars`
        `sets forth` MEANS `s 389(c)(4) What the entity's certificate sets forth` WITH
            `the name and address of its registered agent in this State` IS `it names our registered agent in this State`
            `a general description of the business in which it is engaged` IS `it describes our business`
            `that the filing of the certificate has been duly authorized by any necessary action and does not violate its governing documents or any material agreement or instrument` IS `it states that the filing was duly authorized and violates nothing`
            `a list of the persons authorized to sign the written communications required by subsection (e)` IS `it lists who may sign the written communications of subsection (e)`
            `an affirmance that the transfer is not expressly prohibited under the law by which its internal affairs are governed` IS `it affirms that the transfer is not expressly prohibited`
            `an undertaking that any transfer will take place only in the event of an emergency condition and will continue only so long as the emergency condition, in the judgment of its management, so requires` IS `it undertakes that the transfer will be made only in an emergency condition`

@export Is the translation requirement of section 389(c) met for my entity's documents?
GIVEN `any of the documents is not in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the documents not in English?
      `a translation under oath of the translator is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is a translation, under oath of the translator, attached to it?
      `the Secretary of State has waived the translation requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State waived the translation requirement on the entity's request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(c) Is the translation requirement met` IF
    `s 389(c) the translation requirement is met` `any of the documents is not in English` `a translation under oath of the translator is attached` `the Secretary of State has waived the translation requirement`

@export Must the Secretary of State tell my entity that its documents have been accepted for filing (s 389(c))?
GIVEN `the documents satisfy the requirements of section 389` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the documents satisfy the requirements of section 389?
      `the name of my entity meets the requirements of section 102(a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name of the non-United States entity meet the requirements of section 102(a)(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(c) Must the Secretary of State tell my entity its documents are accepted` IF
    `s 389(c) the Secretary of State must notify the entity that the documents have been accepted for filing` `the documents satisfy the requirements of section 389` `the name of my entity meets the requirements of section 102(a)(1)`

@export Is my entity's name on the Secretary of State's reserved list (s 389(c))?
GIVEN `the documents have been accepted for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State accepted the documents for filing?
      `my entity is in compliance with section 389` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity in compliance with section 389?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(c) Is my entity's name on the reserved list` IF
    `s 389(c) the name of the entity is on the Secretary of State's reserved list` `the documents have been accepted for filing` `my entity is in compliance with section 389`

@export Can other people inspect the documents my entity submitted, under Delaware's Freedom of Information Act (s 389(c))?
GIVEN `my entity has effected a transfer of its domicile` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity effected a transfer of its domicile as provided in section 389?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(c) Can others inspect my entity's documents` IS
    `s 389(c) the document submitted is available for public inspection pursuant to Chapter 100 of Title 29` `my entity has effected a transfer of its domicile`

@export May the Secretary of State waive the 30-day period and the translation requirement for my entity (s 389(c))?
GIVEN `we have asked for the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity requested the waiver?
      `our request is supported by facts justifying the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the request supported by facts, including the existence of an emergency condition, justifying the waiver?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(c) May the Secretary of State waive the 30-day period and the translation requirement` IF
    `s 389(c) the Secretary of State may waive the 30-day period and the translation requirement` `we have asked for the waiver` `our request is supported by facts justifying the waiver`

§§ `389(d) - the annual certificate`

@export Must my entity file the annual certificate (s 389(d))?
GIVEN `my entity is` IS A `s 389(d) Stage of the entity` @desc At what stage is the entity: before the transfer of its domicile, during it, after its domicile has ceased to be in Delaware and it desires to continue to be subject to a transfer, or after and it does not?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(d) Must my entity file the annual certificate` IS
    `s 389(d) the entity must file the annual certificate` `my entity is`

@export By what date in a year must my entity file the annual certificate (s 389(d))?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc For which year? (for example 2026)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 389(d) By what date must my entity file the annual certificate` IS
    `s 389(d) the last day for filing the annual certificate in the year` `the year`

@export Is my entity's annual certificate in order (s 389(d))?
GIVEN `it is executed by an appropriate officer or director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate executed by an appropriate officer or director of the entity?
      `it certifies that the documents remain in force or attaches amendments or supplements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify that the documents submitted remain in full force and effect, or attach any amendments or supplements, translated as section 389(c) requires?
      `the filing fee we paid, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much filing fee did the entity pay with it, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(d) Is my entity's annual certificate in order` IF
    `s 389(d) the annual certificate is in order` certificate
    WHERE
        certificate MEANS `s 389(d) What the annual certificate does` WITH
            `certificate is executed by an appropriate officer or director of the entity` IS `it is executed by an appropriate officer or director`
            `certificate certifies that the documents remain in full force and effect, or attaches any amendments or supplements, translated as required in subsection (c)` IS `it certifies that the documents remain in force or attaches amendments or supplements`
            `filing fee prescribed under § 391` IS `the filing fee we paid, in dollars`

@export Have my entity's certificates and filings under section 389 become null and void (s 389(d))?
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc For which year? (for example 2026)
      `we have filed the annual certificate for that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity filed the annual certificate for that year?
      `the date we filed it` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (ISO 8601; ignored if you have not filed it)
      `the date I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which date do you ask? (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(d) Have my entity's certificates and filings become void` IF
    `s 389(d) the certificates and filings made pursuant to this section have become null and void` `the year`
        (IF `we have filed the annual certificate for that year` THEN JUST `the date we filed it` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the date I ask about`

@export If my entity's filings have become void, must it make all the submissions of subsection (c) again and pay the examination fee again (s 389(d))?
GIVEN `my entity's filings have become null and void` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the entity's certificates and filings under section 389 become null and void because the annual certificate was not filed on or before March 1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(d) Must my entity start again with all the submissions and the examination fee` IF
    `s 389(d) a proposed transfer is subject to all of the required submissions and the examination fee of subsection (c)` `my entity's filings have become null and void`

§§ `389(e) to (h) - making the transfer, and its effects`

@export Has my entity validly transferred its domicile to Delaware (s 389(e))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State accepted our documents for filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State accepted the documents submitted under section 389(c) for filing?
      `we sent a written communication addressed to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the entity send a written communication to the effect that it transfers its domicile, addressed to the Secretary of State?
      `it was signed by 1 of the persons on our list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it signed by 1 of the persons named on the list filed under section 389(c)(4)d.?
      `it confirms that our certified statements remain true and correct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it confirm that the statements made under section 389(c)(4) remain true and correct?
      `we sent it by the ordinary means of communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent by the ordinary means of communication (and not by telegram, telex, telecopy or another form of writing used because of an emergency)?
      `emergency conditions have affected the ordinary means of communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have emergency conditions affected the ordinary means of communication?
      `the date we sent it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the entity send the written communication? (ISO 8601)
      `a duly signed duplicate has been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State received a duly signed duplicate?
      `the date the duplicate was received` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (ISO 8601; ignored if no duplicate has been received)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(e) Has my entity validly transferred its domicile` IF
    `s 389(e) the entity has validly transferred its domicile to this State`
        `the Secretary of State accepted our documents for filing`
        `we sent a written communication addressed to the Secretary of State`
        `it was signed by 1 of the persons on our list`
        `it confirms that our certified statements remain true and correct`
        `we sent it by the ordinary means of communication`
        `emergency conditions have affected the ordinary means of communication`
        `the date we sent it`
        (IF `a duly signed duplicate has been received` THEN JUST `the date the duplicate was received` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Must the Secretary of State record my entity's transfer of domicile (s 389(e))?
GIVEN `my entity has validly transferred its domicile` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity validly transferred its domicile to Delaware under section 389(e)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(e) Must the Secretary of State record the transfer` IF
    `s 389(e) the records of the Secretary of State must reflect the transfer` `my entity has validly transferred its domicile`

@export Must the Secretary of State certify that my entity has filed everything and paid every fee, once I pay the fee (s 389(e))?
GIVEN `we have paid the fee prescribed under section 391` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity paid the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under section 391?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(e) Must the Secretary of State certify that my entity has filed and paid everything` IF
    `s 389(e) the Secretary of State must certify that the entity has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` `we have paid the fee prescribed under section 391`

@export Is the Secretary of State's certificate prima facie evidence of my entity's transfer of domicile (s 389(e))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State issued the certificate that the entity has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(e) Is the Secretary of State's certificate prima facie evidence of the transfer` IF
    `s 389(e) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the transfer of the domicile into this State` `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate`

@export After the transfer, does my entity keep a power it had under the law governing its internal affairs (s 389(f))?
GIVEN `my entity has transferred its domicile to Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity transferred its domicile to Delaware under section 389?
      `the laws of Delaware expressly prohibit that power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the laws of Delaware expressly prohibit that power?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(f) Does my entity keep the power it had` IS
    `s 389(f) the entity has the power that it had immediately prior to the transfer` `my entity has transferred its domicile to Delaware` `the laws of Delaware expressly prohibit that power`

@export May I manage the business and affairs of my entity under the law of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs after the transfer (s 389(f))?
GIVEN `my entity has transferred its domicile to Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity transferred its domicile to Delaware under section 389?
      `I am a director or officer designated under section 389(c)(3), or a successor of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or officer designated under section 389(c)(3), or a successor of one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(f) May I manage my entity under the law governing its internal affairs` IS
    `s 389(f) the person may manage the business and affairs of the entity in accordance with the laws of the jurisdiction governing its internal affairs` `my entity has transferred its domicile to Delaware` `I am a director or officer designated under section 389(c)(3), or a successor of one`

@export Is my entity treated as doing business in Delaware, for section 371, because of activity under section 389 (s 389(f))?
GIVEN `the activity is conducted pursuant to section 389` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the activity conducted pursuant to section 389?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(f) Is my entity treated as doing business in Delaware` IS
    `s 389(f) the activity is deemed to be doing business within this State for purposes of § 371` `the activity is conducted pursuant to section 389`

@export Which version of the foreign law is meant by a reference in section 389 to the law governing my entity's internal affairs (s 389(f))?
GIVEN `my entity has transferred its domicile into Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity transferred its domicile into Delaware?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 389(f) Version of the law governing the internal affairs`
DECIDE `s 389(f) Which version of the foreign law is meant` IS
    `s 389(f) the version of the law to which a reference in this section is a reference` `my entity has transferred its domicile into Delaware`

@export In a Delaware court, can my entity be treated as an enemy because of where it is governed (s 389(g))?
GIVEN `the question arises in an action in the courts of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the question arise in an action in the courts of Delaware?
      `my entity has the Secretary of State's certificate of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity obtained the certificate of the Secretary of State referred to in section 389(e)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(g) Can my entity be treated as an enemy` IS
    `s 389(g) the entity is deemed to be an enemy person or entity` `the question arises in an action in the courts of Delaware` `my entity has the Secretary of State's certificate of transfer`

@export Does the transfer change an obligation or liability my entity incurred before it (s 389(h))?
GIVEN `the obligation or liability was incurred before the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the obligation or liability incurred before the transfer of domicile?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(h) Does the transfer leave my entity's earlier obligation alone` IS
    `s 389(h) the transfer leaves the obligation or liability unaffected` `the obligation or liability was incurred before the transfer`

§§ `389(i) to (k) - dividends, service of process, withdrawal`

-- s 389(i). The directors' power and the holder's liability to it: one rule, asked from each side.
@export May the directors withhold the dividend or distribution payable to me, a holder of equity interests in the entity (s 389(i))?
GIVEN `the entity has transferred its domicile into Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity transferred its domicile into Delaware under section 389?
      `the amount is a dividend or other distribution payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount a dividend or other distribution payable to you as a holder of equity interests?
      `the directors have determined that I will not have the full benefit of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors determined that you will not have the full benefit of the payment?
      `the directors have made provision to retain it in escrow or similar for my benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors made provision for the retention of the withheld payment in escrow, or under some similar arrangement, for your benefit?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(i) May the directors withhold my dividend` IF
    `s 389(i) the directors may withhold the amount payable to the holder` `the entity has transferred its domicile into Delaware` `the amount is a dividend or other distribution payable to me` `the directors have determined that I will not have the full benefit of the payment` `the directors have made provision to retain it in escrow or similar for my benefit`

@export As a director of the entity, may I withhold a dividend or distribution from a holder of equity interests (s 389(i))?
GIVEN `the entity has transferred its domicile into Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity transferred its domicile into Delaware under section 389?
      `the amount is a dividend or other distribution payable to the holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount a dividend or other distribution payable to a holder of equity interests?
      `we the directors determine that the holder will not have the full benefit of the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors determine that the holder will not have the full benefit of the payment?
      `we the directors provide for retention in escrow or under a similar arrangement for the holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the directors make provision for the retention of the withheld payment in escrow, or under some similar arrangement, for the benefit of the holder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(i) May I as a director withhold the amount` IF
    `s 389(i) the directors may withhold the amount payable to the holder` `the entity has transferred its domicile into Delaware` `the amount is a dividend or other distribution payable to the holder` `we the directors determine that the holder will not have the full benefit of the payment` `we the directors provide for retention in escrow or under a similar arrangement for the holder`

@export Can process, orders, rules and notices be served on my entity as if it were a Delaware corporation (s 389(j))?
GIVEN `my entity has transferred its domicile into Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity transferred its domicile into Delaware under section 389?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(j) Can process be served on my entity as on a Delaware corporation` IS
    `s 389(j) process, orders, rules and notices may be served on the entity pursuant to § 321 as if it were a corporation of this State` `my entity has transferred its domicile into Delaware`

@export As a director, have I done what section 389 requires before I take office (s 389(j))?
GIVEN `I have agreed in writing to be amenable to service of process and the jurisdiction of the courts of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you agreed in writing that you will be amenable to service of process by the same means as, and subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of Delaware to the same extent as, directors of corporations of Delaware?
      `that agreement was submitted to the Secretary of State for filing before I took office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement submitted to the Secretary of State for filing before you took office?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(j) Have I done what is required before taking office` IF
    `s 389(j) the director has done what the section requires before taking office` `I have agreed in writing to be amenable to service of process and the jurisdiction of the courts of Delaware` `that agreement was submitted to the Secretary of State for filing before I took office`

@export Is my entity's application to withdraw from Delaware complete (s 389(k))?
GIVEN `it is accompanied by a resolution of our directors authorizing the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application accompanied by a resolution of the directors authorizing the withdrawal?
      `it is accompanied by a certificate of the highest diplomatic or consular official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it accompanied by a certificate of the highest diplomatic or consular official of the jurisdiction accredited to the United States indicating that jurisdiction's consent?
      `it contains the entity's agreement to be served with process in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain, or is it accompanied by, the entity's agreement that it may be served with process in Delaware in any proceeding to enforce an obligation arising before its withdrawal?
      `that agreement appoints the Secretary of State as agent for service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that agreement include the appointment of the Secretary of State as the entity's agent to accept service of process?
      `that agreement specifies the address for a copy of the process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the address to which a copy of process served upon the Secretary of State shall be mailed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(k) Is my entity's application to withdraw complete` IF
    `s 389(k) the application to withdraw is complete` application
    WHERE
        application MEANS `s 389(k) What the application to withdraw contains or is accompanied by` WITH
            `resolution of the directors authorizing the withdrawal` IS `it is accompanied by a resolution of our directors authorizing the withdrawal`
            `certificate of the highest diplomatic or consular official of the jurisdiction accredited to the United States indicating its consent` IS `it is accompanied by a certificate of the highest diplomatic or consular official`
            `agreement that the entity may be served with process in this State on obligations arising prior to withdrawal` IS `it contains the entity's agreement to be served with process in Delaware`
            `appointment of the Secretary of State as the agent of the entity to accept service of process in such a proceeding` IS `that agreement appoints the Secretary of State as agent for service`
            `the address to which a copy of process served upon the Secretary of State shall be mailed` IS `that agreement specifies the address for a copy of the process`

@export Must the Secretary of State file my entity's application to withdraw (s 389(k))?
GIVEN `the application to withdraw is complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application to withdraw complete?
      `we have paid any fees and taxes owed to Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity paid any fees and taxes owed to Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(k) Must the Secretary of State file my entity's application` IF
    `s 389(k) the Secretary of State must file the application to withdraw` `the application to withdraw is complete` `we have paid any fees and taxes owed to Delaware`

@export Has my entity's domicile ceased to be in Delaware (s 389(k))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has filed our application to withdraw` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State filed the entity's application to withdraw?
      `the time I ask about is at or after the time of filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the time you ask about at or after the time of filing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 389(k) Has my entity's domicile ceased to be in Delaware` IF
    `s 389(k) the domicile of the entity has ceased to be in this State` `the Secretary of State has filed our application to withdraw` `the time I ask about is at or after the time of filing`

§ `Section 390 - moving a Delaware corporation out of Delaware`

-- SITUATION: your Delaware corporation is transferring to, or domesticating or continuing in, a foreign jurisdiction (and may elect to keep its Delaware existence too).

§§ `390(a), (b) - may it move; the resolution, the meeting, the vote and the certificate`

-- s 390(a)(1).
@export Is this place a foreign jurisdiction within the meaning of section 390 (s 390(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the place is` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Where would the corporation go: this State, another jurisdiction of the United States, or a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(a)(1) Is this place a foreign jurisdiction` IF
    `s 390(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` `the place is`

-- s 390(a).
@export May my Delaware corporation transfer to, or domesticate or continue in, a foreign jurisdiction (s 390(a))?
GIVEN `my corporation exists under the laws of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation exist under the laws of Delaware?
      `the place it would go to is` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Where would the corporation go: this State, another jurisdiction of the United States, or a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States?
      `the board has adopted the resolution and submitted it to the stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board of directors adopted the resolution that subsection (b) requires and submitted it to the stockholders as it requires?
      `the stockholders have approved, or no stockholder vote is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the stockholders approved, or is no vote of the stockholders necessary (section 390(h))?
      `the certificate required by subsection (b) has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the certificate of transfer, or of transfer and domestic continuance, been filed with the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(a) May my corporation move out of Delaware` IF
    `s 390(a) the corporation may transfer to, or domesticate or continue in, the foreign jurisdiction` `my corporation exists under the laws of Delaware` `the place it would go to is` `the board has adopted the resolution and submitted it to the stockholders` `the stockholders have approved, or no stockholder vote is necessary` `the certificate required by subsection (b) has been filed`

@export Which certificate must my corporation file with the Secretary of State to move out (s 390(a), (b))?
GIVEN `my corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation elect to continue its existence as a corporation of Delaware after the move?
GIVETH A `s 390(b) Certificate to be filed with the Secretary of State`
DECIDE `s 390(b) Which certificate must my corporation file` IS
    `s 390(b) the certificate that the corporation files` `my corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of Delaware`

-- s 390(b). The board's resolution.
@export Has the board adopted the resolution that section 390(b) requires (s 390(b))?
GIVEN `the board adopted a resolution approving the move` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board of directors adopted a resolution approving the transfer, domestication or continuance?
      `it specifies the foreign jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution specify the foreign jurisdiction to which the corporation shall be transferred or in which it shall be domesticated or continued?
      `it states that the corporation's Delaware existence is to continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the corporation's existence as a corporation of Delaware is to continue? (Needed only if the corporation elects to continue.)
      `it recommends approval by the stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it recommend the approval of the move by the stockholders?
      `the plan was approved together with the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance is to be adopted, was it approved together with the resolution?
      `my corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation elect to continue its existence as a corporation of Delaware?
      `a plan is to be adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance to be adopted under section 390(j)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b) Has the board adopted the resolution as required` IF
    `s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` resolution `my corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of Delaware` `a plan is to be adopted`
    WHERE
        resolution MEANS `s 390(b) Resolution of the board of directors` WITH
            `resolution approving the transfer, domestication or continuance adopted by the board of directors` IS `the board adopted a resolution approving the move`
            `resolution specifies the foreign jurisdiction` IS `it specifies the foreign jurisdiction`
            `resolution states that the corporation's existence as a corporation of this State is to continue` IS `it states that the corporation's Delaware existence is to continue`
            `resolution recommends approval by the stockholders` IS `it recommends approval by the stockholders`
            `plan of transfer, domestication or continuance approved together with the resolution` IS `the plan was approved together with the resolution`

-- s 390(b). The meeting and the notice: the stockholder's claim to proper notice, and the corporation's duty to give it.
@export Was the notice of the stockholders' meeting on the move given as section 390(b) requires?
GIVEN `the resolution is submitted at an annual or special meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution to be submitted to the stockholders at an annual or special meeting?
      `the notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the time, place and purpose of the meeting?
      `the notice goes to each holder of stock, voting or nonvoting, at the address on the records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the address of the stockholder as it appears on the corporation's records?
      `the notice was given on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-10)
      `the meeting is on` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting? (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b) Was the notice of the meeting given as required` IF
    `s 390(b) the notice of the meeting was given as required` notice
    WHERE
        notice MEANS `s 390(b) Notice of the meeting of the stockholders` WITH
            `meeting at which the resolution is submitted is an annual or special meeting` IS `the resolution is submitted at an annual or special meeting`
            `notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting` IS `the notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting`
            `notice is given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the address on the corporation's records` IS `the notice goes to each holder of stock, voting or nonvoting, at the address on the records`
            `date on which the notice was given` IS `the notice was given on`
            `date of the meeting` IS `the meeting is on`

@export Have the stockholders adopted the resolution to move (s 390(b))?
GIVEN `the votes in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favor of adopting the resolution? (votes, not shares, where the certificate gives more or less than one vote per share)
      `the outstanding stock entitled to vote, in votes` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes does the outstanding stock entitled to vote carry?
      `the move is as a partnership with general partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation transferring, domesticating or continuing as a partnership having 1 or more general partners?
      `stockholders who will become general partners` IS A NUMBER @desc How many stockholders will become a general partner of the partnership as a result? (0 if the move is not as a partnership)
      `of those, the number who approve` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those stockholders, how many approve?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b) Have the stockholders adopted the resolution` IS
    `s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` `the votes in favor` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote, in votes` `the move is as a partnership with general partners` `stockholders who will become general partners` `of those, the number who approve`

@export As a stockholder, must I approve the move myself because I will become a general partner (s 390(b))?
GIVEN `the move is as a partnership with general partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation transferring, domesticating or continuing as a partnership having 1 or more general partners?
      `I will become a general partner as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you become a general partner of that partnership as a result of the move?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b) Must I approve the move myself` IF
    `s 390(b) the approval of the stockholder is required for the authorization, in addition to the vote` `the move is as a partnership with general partners` `I will become a general partner as a result`

@export Does the certificate my corporation files to move out certify everything that section 390(b) requires?
GIVEN `the certificate is` IS A `s 390(b) Certificate to be filed with the Secretary of State` @desc Which certificate is it: a certificate of transfer, or a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance?
      `it gives the name of the corporation and any original name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify the name of the corporation and, if it has been changed, the name under which it was originally incorporated?
      `it gives the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify the date of filing of the corporation's original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State?
      `it names the foreign jurisdiction and the resulting entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify the foreign jurisdiction and the name of the resulting entity?
      `it certifies that the move has been approved in accordance with section 390` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify that the transfer, domestication or continuance has been approved in accordance with section 390?
      `it certifies that the Delaware existence shall cease when the certificate is effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a certificate of transfer: does it certify that the existence of the corporation as a corporation of Delaware shall cease when the certificate becomes effective?
      `it contains the agreement to be served with process and appoints the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a certificate of transfer: does it contain the corporation's agreement that it may be served with process in Delaware for obligations arising while it was a Delaware corporation, irrevocably appointing the Secretary of State as its agent and specifying the address for mailing a copy of process?
      `it certifies that the corporation will continue to exist as a Delaware corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance: does it certify that the corporation will continue to exist as a corporation of Delaware after the certificate becomes effective?
      `it certifies that all provisions of the plan shall be approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a plan is adopted: does it certify that all provisions of the plan shall be approved in accordance with section 390?
      `a plan is adopted under subsection (j)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance adopted under section 390(j)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b) Does my corporation's certificate certify everything required` IF
    `s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` `the certificate is` certifies `a plan is adopted under subsection (j)`
    WHERE
        certifies MEANS `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies` WITH
            `name of the corporation and, if it has been changed, the name under which it was originally incorporated` IS `it gives the name of the corporation and any original name`
            `date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State` IS `it gives the date of filing of the original certificate of incorporation`
            `foreign jurisdiction and the name of the resulting entity` IS `it names the foreign jurisdiction and the resulting entity`
            `that the transfer, domestication or continuance has been approved in accordance with this section` IS `it certifies that the move has been approved in accordance with section 390`
            `that the existence of the corporation as a corporation of this State shall cease when the certificate of transfer becomes effective` IS `it certifies that the Delaware existence shall cease when the certificate is effective`
            `agreement that the corporation may be served with process in this State, irrevocably appointing the Secretary of State as its agent and specifying an address` IS `it contains the agreement to be served with process and appoints the Secretary of State`
            `that the corporation will continue to exist as a corporation of this State after the certificate becomes effective` IS `it certifies that the corporation will continue to exist as a Delaware corporation`
            `that all provisions of the plan shall be approved in accordance with this section` IS `it certifies that all provisions of the plan shall be approved`

§§ `390(b)(5) - service of process on a corporation that has transferred out`

-- SITUATION: a corporation has transferred out of Delaware and is being sued in Delaware, or you are suing it.

@export May the address given for the mailing of process be the address of my corporation's registered agent (s 390(b)(5))?
GIVEN `the address specified is that of the corporation's registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the address specified in the certificate of transfer for the mailing of a copy of process that of the corporation's registered agent?
      `the registered agent's written consent is filed with the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the written consent of the corporation's registered agent filed along with the certificate of transfer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b)(5) Is the address given for the mailing of process permitted` IF
    `s 390(b)(5) the address specified for the mailing of a copy of process is permitted` `the address specified is that of the corporation's registered agent` `the registered agent's written consent is filed with the certificate`

@export May process be served upon the Secretary of State by electronic transmission on a corporation that has transferred out (s 390(b)(5))?
GIVEN `the service is made as the Secretary of State prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service by electronic transmission made as prescribed by the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b)(5) May process be served by electronic transmission` IF
    `s 390(b)(5) process may be served upon the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` `the service is made as the Secretary of State prescribes`

@export To what address will the Secretary of State mail the letter telling my corporation that process has been served (s 390(b)(5))?
GIVEN `the address in our certificate of transfer` IS A STRING @desc What address is specified in the certificate of transfer for the mailing of a copy of process?
      `we have designated a different address in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for this purpose?
      `the last address we designated` IS A STRING @desc If so, what is the last address designated? (ignored if none)
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `s 390(b)(5) To what address will the Secretary of State mail the letter` IS
    `s 390(b)(5) the address to which the Secretary of State mails the letter notifying the corporation of the service`
        `the address in our certificate of transfer`
        (IF `we have designated a different address in writing` THEN JUST `the last address we designated` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Was the Secretary of State's letter telling my corporation of the service sent as section 390(b)(5) requires?
GIVEN `it was sent by a mail or courier service that records mailing or deposit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier?
      `there is a record of delivery signed for by the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient?
      `it enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b)(5) Was the letter sent as required` IF
    `s 390(b)(5) the letter notifying the corporation of the service is sent as required` `it was sent by a mail or courier service that records mailing or deposit` `there is a record of delivery signed for by the recipient` `it enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served`

@export How much must a plaintiff pay the Secretary of State on serving process on a corporation that has transferred out, in dollars (s 390(b)(5))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 390(b)(5) How much must I pay the Secretary of State on service` IS
    `s 390(b)(5) the sum that the plaintiff pays the Secretary of State on service`

@export As the plaintiff, have I done what section 390(b)(5) requires of me when serving the Secretary of State?
GIVEN `I served process and any other papers in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve process and any other papers in duplicate?
      `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under section 390(b)(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to section 390(b)(5)?
      `the sum I paid the Secretary of State, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you pay the Secretary of State on service, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b)(5) Have I done what the plaintiff's duty on service requires` IF
    `s 390(b)(5) the plaintiff has done what the duty on service requires` `I served process and any other papers in duplicate` `I notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under section 390(b)(5)` `the sum I paid the Secretary of State, in dollars`

@export Is the sum a plaintiff paid the Secretary of State taxed as part of the costs (s 390(b)(5))?
GIVEN `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plaintiff prevail in the proceeding?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b)(5) Is the sum I paid taxed as part of the costs` IS
    `s 390(b)(5) the sum paid to the Secretary of State is taxed as part of the costs` `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding`

@export Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record of a service of process (s 390(b)(5))?
GIVEN `the years since the Secretary of State received the service` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years have passed since the Secretary of State received the service of process?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(b)(5) Is the Secretary of State still required to keep the record` IS
    `s 390(b)(5) the Secretary of State is required to retain the record of the service` `the years since the Secretary of State received the service`

§§ `390(c) to (g) - when my corporation stops being a Delaware corporation, and what it leaves alone`

@export Must the Secretary of State certify that my corporation has filed everything and paid every fee, once it has filed a certificate of transfer (s 390(c))?
GIVEN `a certificate of transfer, not one of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of transfer (not a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance) filed in accordance with section 390(b)?
      `all fees prescribed under the title were paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were all fees prescribed under this title paid to the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(c) Must the Secretary of State certify that my corporation has filed and paid everything` IF
    `s 390(c) the Secretary of State must certify that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` `a certificate of transfer, not one of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed` `all fees prescribed under the title were paid`

@export Has my corporation ceased to exist as a corporation of Delaware (s 390(c))?
GIVEN `a certificate of transfer, not one of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of transfer (not a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance) filed in accordance with section 390(b)?
      `all fees prescribed under the title were paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were all fees prescribed under this title paid to the Secretary of State?
      `the time I ask about is at or after the time the certificate becomes effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the time you ask about at or after the time the certificate of transfer becomes effective in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(c) Has my corporation ceased to exist in Delaware` IF
    `s 390(c) the corporation has ceased to exist as a corporation of this State` `a certificate of transfer, not one of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed` `all fees prescribed under the title were paid` `the time I ask about is at or after the time the certificate becomes effective`

@export Is the Secretary of State's certificate prima facie evidence that my corporation moved out (s 390(c))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State issued the certificate that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(c) Is the Secretary of State's certificate prima facie evidence of the move` IF
    `s 390(c) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the transfer, domestication or continuance out of this State` `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate`

@export Does the move change an obligation, liability, personal liability or choice of law that arose before it (s 390(d))?
GIVEN `the matter is` IS A `s 390(d) Matter that the transfer leaves unaffected` @desc What is in question: an obligation or liability incurred before the move, a person's personal liability incurred before it, the choice of law for matters arising before it, or another matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(d) Does the move leave my earlier obligation or liability alone` IS
    `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance leaves the matter unaffected` `the matter is`

@export Must my corporation wind up its affairs because it moves out of Delaware (s 390(d))?
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it otherwise agreed (for example in an agreement with the stockholders) that the corporation must wind up?
      `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation otherwise provide?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(d) Must my corporation wind up` IS
    `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance requires the corporation to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets under this title` `it is otherwise agreed` `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides`

@export Is my corporation's move out of Delaware a dissolution of it (s 390(d))?
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it otherwise agreed that the move is a dissolution?
      `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation otherwise provide?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(d) Is the move a dissolution of my corporation` IS
    `s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance is deemed to constitute a dissolution of the corporation` `it is otherwise agreed` `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides`

@export Does my corporation continue to exist as a Delaware corporation after a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance (s 390(e))?
GIVEN `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance was filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance filed?
      `it has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(e) Does my corporation continue to exist in Delaware` IF
    `s 390(e) the corporation continues to exist as a corporation of this State, with the law of this State applying as before` `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance was filed` `it has become effective`

@export Are my continuing Delaware corporation and the resulting entity a single entity (s 390(e))?
GIVEN `my corporation continues to exist as a Delaware corporation after filing a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation continue to exist as a corporation of Delaware following the filing of a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(e) Are the continuing corporation and the resulting entity a single entity` IS
    `s 390(e) the continuing corporation and the resulting entity constitute a single entity` `my corporation continues to exist as a Delaware corporation after filing a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance`

@export Is the resulting entity the same entity as my corporation after it moves (s 390(f))?
GIVEN `the move has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transfer, domestication or continuance become effective under section 390?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(f) Is the resulting entity the same entity as my corporation` IS
    `s 390(f) the resulting entity is deemed to be the same entity as the corporation, a continuation of its existence` `the move has become effective`

@export In whom do my corporation's rights, property and causes of action remain vested after it moves (s 390(f))?
GIVEN `the move has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transfer, domestication or continuance become effective under section 390?
      `my corporation continues its existence as a Delaware corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation continue its existence as a corporation of Delaware?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 390(f) Who holds or bears after the transfer, domestication or continuance`
DECIDE `s 390(f) In whom do my corporation's rights and property remain vested` IS
    `s 390(f) in whom the rights, privileges, powers, property, debts due and causes of action of the corporation remain vested` `the move has become effective` `my corporation continues its existence as a Delaware corporation`

@export To whom do my corporation's debts, liabilities and duties remain attached after it moves, so that I can enforce them (s 390(f))?
GIVEN `the move has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transfer, domestication or continuance become effective under section 390?
      `my corporation continues its existence as a Delaware corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation continue its existence as a corporation of Delaware?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 390(f) Who holds or bears after the transfer, domestication or continuance`
DECIDE `s 390(f) To whom do my corporation's debts remain attached` IS
    `s 390(f) to whom the debts, liabilities and duties of the corporation remain attached, to be enforced as if incurred by it as the resulting entity` `the move has become effective` `my corporation continues its existence as a Delaware corporation`

@export Is the title to real property that my corporation holds impaired by its move (s 390(f))?
GIVEN `the move has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transfer, domestication or continuance become effective under section 390?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(f) Is my corporation's title to real property impaired by the move` IS
    `s 390(f) title to real property vested in the corporation reverts or is impaired by reason of this title` `the move has become effective`

@export Are my rights as a creditor, and my liens on the corporation's property, preserved after it moves (s 390(f))?
GIVEN `the move has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the transfer, domestication or continuance become effective under section 390?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(f) Are my creditor's rights and liens preserved after the move` IS
    `s 390(f) the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of the corporation are preserved unimpaired` `the move has become effective`

@export Does the move count as a transfer of the corporation's rights, property and debts to the resulting entity (s 390(f))?
GIVEN `the vesting or attaching results from the move` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the vesting of the rights and property, and the attaching of the debts, result from the transfer, domestication or continuance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(f) Does the move count as a transfer to the resulting entity` IS
    `s 390(f) the rights, privileges, powers, interests in property, debts, liabilities and duties are deemed to have been transferred to the resulting entity` `the vesting or attaching results from the move`

@export Can my shares in the corporation be exchanged, converted or cancelled in the move (s 390(g))?
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `s 390(g) Treatment of the shares of the corporation` @desc What would be done to them: exchanged or converted into cash, into property, into shares or securities of the resulting entity, into cash, property or shares of another corporation or entity, or cancelled?
      `it is in connection with a transfer, domestication or continuance under section 390` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this done in connection with a transfer, domestication or continuance under section 390?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(g) Can my shares be so treated in the move` IS
    `s 390(g) the shares of the corporation may be so treated` `the treatment` `it is in connection with a transfer, domestication or continuance under section 390`

§§ `390(h), (i) - is a stockholder vote needed; nonstock corporations`

@export Is a vote of the stockholders necessary to authorize my corporation's move (s 390(h))?
GIVEN `shares have been issued before the board adopted the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had any shares of the corporation's stock been issued before the board of directors adopted the resolution approving the move?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(h) Is a stockholder vote necessary for the move` IF
    `s 390(h) a vote of the stockholders is necessary to authorize the transfer, domestication or continuance` `shares have been issued before the board adopted the resolution`

-- SITUATION for the next five: your corporation is a nonstock corporation.
@export Does the governing body of a nonstock corporation perform the acts that section 390 requires of a board of directors (s 390(i))?
GIVEN `my corporation is of this kind` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(i) Does the governing body perform the board's acts` IS
    `s 390(i) the governing body performs the acts required of the board of directors` `my corporation is of this kind`

@export Who authorizes the move of a nonstock corporation: the members, or the governing body (s 390(i))?
GIVEN `the members are entitled to vote for the election of members of the governing body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the members entitled to vote for the election of members of the governing body?
      `the members may vote on the move or on a merger, consolidation or dissolution under the certificate or bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the members entitled under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws to vote on this move or on a merger, consolidation or dissolution of the corporation?
      `a member is entitled to vote on the move` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any member entitled to vote on the move?
      `there is another holder of a membership interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there another holder of any membership interest in the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 390(i) Who authorizes the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation`
DECIDE `s 390(i) Who authorizes the move of a nonstock corporation` IS
    `s 390(i) who authorizes the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation` `the members are entitled to vote for the election of members of the governing body` `the members may vote on the move or on a merger, consolidation or dissolution under the certificate or bylaws` `a member is entitled to vote on the move` `there is another holder of a membership interest`

@export Has the governing body authorized the move by a majority of its members then in office (s 390(i))?
GIVEN `members of the governing body voting in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the governing body voted in favor of the resolution?
      `members of the governing body then in office` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the governing body are then in office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(i) Has the governing body authorized the move by a majority` IS
    `s 390(i) the governing body has authorized the transfer, domestication or continuance by the vote of a majority of its members then in office` `members of the governing body voting in favor` `members of the governing body then in office`

@export Must the rest of the move of a nonstock corporation conform as nearly as may be to the proceedings for a corporation with capital stock (s 390(i))?
GIVEN `my corporation is of this kind` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(i) Must the proceedings conform to those for a corporation with capital stock` IS
    `s 390(i) the method and proceedings conform as nearly as may be to those prescribed by this section for corporations having capital stock` `my corporation is of this kind`

@export Must my corporation mail notice of its move to the Attorney General of Delaware (s 390(i))?
GIVEN `my corporation is of this kind` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it: a stock corporation, a nonstock corporation with membership interests, a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable, or a charitable nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(i) Must my corporation mail notice to the Attorney General` IF
    `s 390(i) due notice must be mailed to the Attorney General` `my corporation is of this kind`

@export Was my charitable nonstock corporation's notice to the Attorney General mailed in time (s 390(i))?
GIVEN `we mailed the notice to the Attorney General on` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of the corporation's intent mailed to the Attorney General of Delaware? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-09-20)
      `the move is proposed for` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the transfer, domestication or continuance proposed? (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(i) Was the notice to the Attorney General mailed in time` IF
    `s 390(i) the notice to the Attorney General was mailed in time` `we mailed the notice to the Attorney General on` `the move is proposed for`

§§ `390(j), (k) - the plan; restrictions on mergers`

@export May the plan of transfer, domestication or continuance state a given thing (s 390(j))?
GIVEN `the statement` IS A `s 390(j) Statement that a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance may make` @desc What would the plan state?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(j) May the plan state it` IS
    `s 390(j) the plan may state it` `the statement`

@export May a term of the plan of transfer, domestication or continuance depend on facts outside the plan (s 390(j))?
GIVEN `the plan sets out clearly and expressly how those facts operate on its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the plan clearly and expressly set forth the manner in which those facts operate upon the terms of the plan?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(j) May a term of the plan depend on facts outside the plan` IF
    `s 390(j) a term of the plan may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of the plan` `the plan sets out clearly and expressly how those facts operate on its terms`

@export May a term of the plan of transfer, domestication or continuance depend on this kind of fact (s 390(j))?
GIVEN `the fact is` IS A `s 390(j) Kind of fact on which a term of the plan may depend` @desc What kind of fact: the occurrence of an event, a determination or action by a person or body (including the resulting entity or the corporation), or another kind of fact?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 390(j) May a term of the plan depend on this kind of fact` IS
    `s 390(j) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` `the fact is`

-- s 390(k). A stockholder's or a director's question: does a merger restriction I hold or must observe also bind a move out?
@export Does a restriction on mergers in my corporation's certificate of incorporation, or in a stockholders' agreement, also apply to a transfer, domestication or continuance (s 390(k))?
GIVEN `the restriction is found` IS A `s 390(k) Where the restriction is found` @desc Where is the restriction: in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation, or in a voting trust agreement or other written agreement between the corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders?
      `the corporation was incorporated on` IS A DATE @desc If it is in the certificate of incorporation: on what date was the corporation incorporated? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2023-07-31)
      `the agreement came into effect on` IS A DATE @desc If it is in an agreement: on what date did the agreement come into effect? (ISO 8601)
      `it restricts, conditions or prohibits a merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision restrict, condition or prohibit the consummation of a merger or consolidation?
      `it expressly provides otherwise for a transfer, domestication or continuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate or agreement expressly provide otherwise with respect to a transfer, domestication or continuance?
      `it expressly provides for a conversion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it does not so provide, does the certificate or agreement expressly provide with respect to a conversion?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 390(k) How the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance`
DECIDE `s 390(k) Does the merger restriction also apply to a move out` IS
    `s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `the restriction is found` `the corporation was incorporated on` `the agreement came into effect on` `it restricts, conditions or prohibits a merger or consolidation` `it expressly provides otherwise for a transfer, domestication or continuance` `it expressly provides for a conversion`

§ `Section 391 - fees and penalties payable to the Secretary of State`

-- SITUATION: you are filing something with the Secretary of State, asking for a certificate or copy, or have been asked to pay a fee or penalty. Amounts are United States dollars.

§§ `391(a)(1), (2), (3), (4), (b) - fees that depend on the authorized capital stock`

-- s 391(a)(1), (b)(1). Incorporators: what the Secretary of State charges on an original certificate of incorporation.
@export What fee must I pay to file an original certificate of incorporation, in dollars (s 391(a)(1), (b)(1))?
GIVEN `shares having par value that the corporation is authorized to issue` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares having par value is the corporation authorized to issue? (authorized, not outstanding)
      `the par value of each of those shares, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the par value of each of those shares, in dollars? (0 if there are none)
      `shares without par value that the corporation is authorized to issue` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares without par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(1) What fee must I pay to file an original certificate of incorporation` IS
    `s 391(a)(1) the fee on an original certificate of incorporation` capital
    WHERE
        capital MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `shares having par value that the corporation is authorized to issue`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `the par value of each of those shares, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value that the corporation is authorized to issue`

-- s 391(a)(7). The fees that paragraph (a)(7) lays on the instrument, apart from the fee of its own paragraph.
@export What fees does section 391(a)(7) lay on an instrument I file, in dollars (s 391(a)(7))?
GIVEN `it is a certificate of incorporation filed as required by section 102` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a certificate of incorporation filed as required by section 102?
      `a different fee is specifically prescribed for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another paragraph of section 391 specifically prescribe a different fee for the instrument?
      `it is a certificate of dissolution that meets the criteria of section 391(a)(5)b.` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a certificate of dissolution that certifies that the corporation has no assets and has ceased transacting business, has been required to pay only the minimum franchise tax each year, and has paid all franchise taxes and fees?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(7) What fees does paragraph (a)(7) lay on my instrument` IS
    `s 391(a)(7) the fees that paragraph (a)(7) lays on an instrument` `it is a certificate of incorporation filed as required by section 102` `a different fee is specifically prescribed for it` `it is a certificate of dissolution that meets the criteria of section 391(a)(5)b.`

-- s 391(b)(2). Does my amendment count as increasing the authorized capital stock?
@export Does my certificate of amendment, restated certificate or certificate of validation count as increasing the authorized capital stock (s 391(b)(2))?
GIVEN `it increases the number of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate involve an increase in the number of shares?
      `it increases the par value of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it involve an increase in the par value of shares?
      `it changes shares with par value into shares without par value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it change shares with par value into shares without par value?
      `it changes shares without par value into shares with par value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it change shares without par value into shares with par value?
      `par shares after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc After the change, how many shares having par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
      `par value of each after the change, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc After the change, what is the par value of each share having par value, in dollars?
      `shares without par value after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc After the change, how many shares without par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
      `par shares before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc Before the change, how many shares having par value was the corporation authorized to issue?
      `par value of each before the change, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc Before the change, what was the par value of each share having par value, in dollars?
      `shares without par value before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc Before the change, how many shares without par value was the corporation authorized to issue?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(b)(2) Does my certificate count as increasing the authorized capital stock` IF
    `s 391(b)(2) the certificate is considered as increasing the authorized capital stock` change after before
    WHERE
        change MEANS `s 391(b)(2) Change that a certificate makes to the authorized capital stock` WITH
            `increase in the number of shares` IS `it increases the number of shares`
            `increase in the par value of shares` IS `it increases the par value of shares`
            `change of shares with par value into shares without par value` IS `it changes shares with par value into shares without par value`
            `change of shares without par value into shares with par value` IS `it changes shares without par value into shares with par value`
        after MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `par shares after the change`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `par value of each after the change, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value after the change`
        before MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `par shares before the change`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `par value of each before the change, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value before the change`

-- s 391(a)(2), (3), (b)(2). What the Secretary of State charges on an amendment or a restated certificate.
@export What fee must I pay to file a certificate of amendment or a restated certificate, in dollars (s 391(a)(2), (3), (b)(2))?
GIVEN `it increases the number of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate involve an increase in the number of shares?
      `it increases the par value of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it involve an increase in the par value of shares?
      `it changes shares with par value into shares without par value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it change shares with par value into shares without par value?
      `it changes shares without par value into shares with par value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it change shares without par value into shares with par value?
      `par shares after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc After the change, how many shares having par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
      `par value of each after the change, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc After the change, what is the par value of each share having par value, in dollars?
      `shares without par value after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc After the change, how many shares without par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
      `par shares before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc Before the change, how many shares having par value was the corporation authorized to issue?
      `par value of each before the change, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc Before the change, what was the par value of each share having par value, in dollars?
      `shares without par value before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc Before the change, how many shares without par value was the corporation authorized to issue?
      `my corporation is an exempt corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation an exempt corporation, as defined in section 501(b) of this title?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(2) or (3) What fee must I pay to file my amendment or restated certificate` IS
    `s 391(a)(2) or (3) the fee on a certificate of amendment or a restated certificate` change after before `my corporation is an exempt corporation`
    WHERE
        change MEANS `s 391(b)(2) Change that a certificate makes to the authorized capital stock` WITH
            `increase in the number of shares` IS `it increases the number of shares`
            `increase in the par value of shares` IS `it increases the par value of shares`
            `change of shares with par value into shares without par value` IS `it changes shares with par value into shares without par value`
            `change of shares without par value into shares with par value` IS `it changes shares without par value into shares with par value`
        after MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `par shares after the change`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `par value of each after the change, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value after the change`
        before MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `par shares before the change`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `par value of each before the change, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value before the change`

@export What fee must I pay to file any other certificate relating to corporations that section 391 does not otherwise provide for, in dollars (s 391(a)(3))?
GIVEN `my corporation is an exempt corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation an exempt corporation, as defined in section 501(b) of this title?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(3) What fee must I pay to file any other certificate` IS
    `s 391(a)(3) the fee on any other certificate relating to corporations, not otherwise provided for` `my corporation is an exempt corporation`

-- s 391(a)(4). Two or more corporations merging.
@export What fee must I pay to file a certificate of merger or consolidation of two or more corporations, in dollars (s 391(a)(4))?
GIVEN `par shares of the new corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares having par value is the corporation created by the merger or consolidation authorized to issue?
      `par value of each of the new corporation's shares, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the par value of each of those shares, in dollars?
      `shares without par value of the new corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares without par value is it authorized to issue?
      `total par value of the constituent corporations' shares having par value together, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total par value (number of shares times par value each), in dollars, of the shares having par value that all the constituent corporations are together authorized to issue?
      `shares without par value of the constituent corporations together` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares without par value are all the constituent corporations together authorized to issue?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(4) What fee must I pay to file a certificate of merger or consolidation` IS
    `s 391(a)(4) the fee on a certificate of merger or consolidation, from the aggregate figures` capital `total par value of the constituent corporations' shares having par value together, in dollars` `shares without par value of the constituent corporations together`
    WHERE
        capital MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `par shares of the new corporation`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `par value of each of the new corporation's shares, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value of the new corporation`

@export What is the total payable on a certificate of merger or consolidation when another law of Delaware also requires a tax or fee of a constituent that is not a corporation, in dollars (s 391(a)(4))?
GIVEN `the fee under section 391(a)(4)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fee under section 391(a)(4), in dollars?
      `the tax or fee that another law of Delaware requires of a constituent that is not a corporation` IS A NUMBER @desc What tax or fee does another law of Delaware require of a constituent entity that is not a corporation, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(4) What is the total payable with another law's tax or fee` IS
    `s 391(a)(4) the total payable on the certificate of merger or consolidation, with the tax or fee of another law` `the fee under section 391(a)(4)` `the tax or fee that another law of Delaware requires of a constituent that is not a corporation`

§§ `391(a)(5) to (a)(29) - fees for other papers and services`

@export What fee must I pay to file a certificate of dissolution, in dollars (s 391(a)(5))?
GIVEN `it certifies that the corporation has no assets and has ceased transacting business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of dissolution certify that the corporation has no assets and has ceased transacting business?
      `it certifies that for each year the corporation has been required to pay only the minimum franchise tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify that, for each year since its incorporation in Delaware, the corporation has been required to pay only the minimum franchise tax then prescribed by section 503?
      `it certifies that the corporation has paid all franchise taxes and fees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify that the corporation has paid all franchise taxes and fees due to or assessable by Delaware through the end of the year in which the certificate is filed?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(5) What fee must I pay to file a certificate of dissolution` IS
    `s 391(a)(5) the fee on a certificate of dissolution` certification
    WHERE
        certification MEANS `s 391(a)(5) What a certificate of dissolution certifies` WITH
            `certifies that the corporation has no assets and has ceased transacting business` IS `it certifies that the corporation has no assets and has ceased transacting business`
            `certifies that the corporation, for each year since its incorporation in this State, has been required to pay only the minimum franchise tax then prescribed by § 503` IS `it certifies that for each year the corporation has been required to pay only the minimum franchise tax`
            `certifies that the corporation has paid all franchise taxes and fees due to or assessable by this State through the end of the year in which the certificate is filed` IS `it certifies that the corporation has paid all franchise taxes and fees`

@export What is the most I can be charged under section 391(a) to file this paper or obtain this service, in dollars (s 391(a)(6), (8), (11), (12), (14), (16), (17), (20), (21), (24), (25), (27), (29))?
GIVEN `the paper or service is` IS A `s 391(a) Paper or service whose fee is one stated amount or ceiling` @desc Which paper or service is it? The fee of each is one stated amount, or a ceiling where section 391(a) says "up to".
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a) What is the most I can be charged for this paper or service` IS
    `s 391(a) the most that may be charged under the paragraph for the paper or service` `the paper or service is`

@export Is the amount for this paper or service only a ceiling, so that the Secretary of State's own schedule may set less (s 391(a))?
GIVEN `the paper or service is` IS A `s 391(a) Paper or service whose fee is one stated amount or ceiling` @desc Which paper or service is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(a) Is the amount only a ceiling` IF
    `s 391(a) the amount stated for the paper or service is only a ceiling` `the paper or service is`

@export What fee must I pay to file the annual franchise tax report of a corporation, in dollars (s 391(a)(18))?
GIVEN `my corporation is an exempt corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation an exempt corporation, as defined in section 501(b) of this title?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(18) What fee must I pay to file the annual franchise tax report` IS
    `s 391(a)(18) the fee on an annual franchise tax report of a corporation` `my corporation is an exempt corporation`

@export What is the total fee an exempt corporation pays to file a certificate of change of registered agent or registered office or a certificate of revival, in dollars (s 391(a)(23))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(23) What do I pay as an exempt corporation to change my registered agent or office or to revive` IS
    `s 391(a)(23) the total fees an exempt corporation pays on a certificate of change of registered agent or registered office or a certificate of revival`

@export What fee must a foreign corporation pay to file its annual report, in dollars (s 391(a)(8))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(8) What fee must a foreign corporation pay to file its annual report` IS
    `s 391(a)(8) the fee on the annual report of a foreign corporation doing business in this State`

@export Does a foreign corporation owe the penalty of section 391(a)(8) for filing its annual report late?
GIVEN `the year of the annual report` IS A NUMBER @desc For which year is the annual report? (for example 2025)
      `we have filed the annual report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the foreign corporation filed the annual report with the Secretary of State?
      `the date we filed it` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (ISO 8601; ignored if not yet filed)
      `the date I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which date do you ask? (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(a)(8) Does a foreign corporation owe the late penalty` IF
    `s 391(a)(8) the foreign corporation owes the penalty for the year` `the year of the annual report`
        (IF `we have filed the annual report` THEN JUST `the date we filed it` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the date I ask about`

@export What is the penalty for failing to file a foreign corporation's annual report on or before June 30, in dollars (s 391(a)(8))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(8) What is the late penalty` IS
    `s 391(a)(8) the penalty for failing to file the annual report on or before June 30`

@export What fee must I pay for recording and indexing papers required to be recorded, at one cent a line, in dollars (s 391(a)(9))?
GIVEN `the number of lines` IS A NUMBER @desc How many lines are to be recorded and indexed?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(9) What fee must I pay for recording and indexing` IS
    `s 391(a)(9) the fee for recording and indexing articles of association and other papers required to be recorded` `the number of lines`

@export What fee must I pay for certified copies of a paper on file, in dollars (s 391(a)(10))?
GIVEN `the number of copies I want certified` IS A NUMBER @desc How many copies do you want certified?
      `the number of pages of the document` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages does the document have?
      `the Secretary of State provides the copies to be certified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the Secretary of State provide the copies of the document to be certified?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(10) What fee must I pay for certified copies` IS
    `s 391(a)(10) the fee for certifying copies of a paper on file` `the number of copies I want certified` `the number of pages of the document` `the Secretary of State provides the copies to be certified`

@export What fee must I pay for a certificate of change of address or change of name of a registered agent, in dollars (s 391(a)(13))?
GIVEN `the other fees charged as on filing a certificate of incorporation` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the same fees for receiving, filing, indexing, copying and certifying as are charged in the case of filing a certificate of incorporation, in dollars? (Section 391 does not total them; state the sum you are charged.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(13) What fee must I pay for a change of address or name of a registered agent` IS
    `s 391(a)(13) the fee on a certificate of change of address or change of name of registered agent` `the other fees charged as on filing a certificate of incorporation`

@export What fee must a registered agent pay to resign without appointing a successor, in dollars (s 391(a)(15))?
GIVEN `the number of corporations whose registered agent resigns by the certificate` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many corporations does the registered agent resign by the certificate?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(15) What fee must a registered agent pay to resign without a successor` IS
    `s 391(a)(15) the fee on a certificate of resignation of a registered agent without appointment of a successor` `the number of corporations whose registered agent resigns by the certificate`

@export What fee must I pay for a certificate of domestication and certificate of incorporation under section 388, in dollars (s 391(a)(19))?
GIVEN `shares having par value that the corporation is authorized to issue` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares having par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
      `the par value of each of those shares, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the par value of each of those shares, in dollars? (0 if there are none)
      `shares without par value that the corporation is authorized to issue` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares without par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(19) What fee must I pay for a certificate of domestication and certificate of incorporation` IS
    `s 391(a)(19) the fee on a certificate of domestication and certificate of incorporation prescribed in § 388(d)` capital
    WHERE
        capital MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `shares having par value that the corporation is authorized to issue`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `the par value of each of those shares, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value that the corporation is authorized to issue`

@export What fee must I pay for a certificate of conversion and certificate of incorporation under section 265, in dollars (s 391(a)(26))?
GIVEN `shares having par value that the corporation is authorized to issue` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares having par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
      `the par value of each of those shares, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the par value of each of those shares, in dollars? (0 if there are none)
      `shares without par value that the corporation is authorized to issue` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares without par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(26) What fee must I pay for a certificate of conversion and certificate of incorporation` IS
    `s 391(a)(26) the fee on a certificate of conversion and certificate of incorporation prescribed in § 265` capital
    WHERE
        capital MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `shares having par value that the corporation is authorized to issue`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `the par value of each of those shares, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value that the corporation is authorized to issue`

@export What fee must I pay for a certificate of validation under section 204, in dollars (s 391(a)(28))?
GIVEN `it increases the number of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of validation involve an increase in the number of shares?
      `it increases the par value of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it involve an increase in the par value of shares?
      `it changes shares with par value into shares without par value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it change shares with par value into shares without par value?
      `it changes shares without par value into shares with par value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it change shares without par value into shares with par value?
      `par shares after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc After the change, how many shares having par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
      `par value of each after the change, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc After the change, what is the par value of each share having par value, in dollars?
      `shares without par value after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc After the change, how many shares without par value is the corporation authorized to issue?
      `par shares before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc Before the change, how many shares having par value was the corporation authorized to issue?
      `par value of each before the change, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc Before the change, what was the par value of each share having par value, in dollars?
      `shares without par value before the change` IS A NUMBER @desc Before the change, how many shares without par value was the corporation authorized to issue?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(28) What fee must I pay for a certificate of validation` IS
    `s 391(a)(28) the fee on a certificate of validation prescribed in § 204` change after before
    WHERE
        change MEANS `s 391(b)(2) Change that a certificate makes to the authorized capital stock` WITH
            `increase in the number of shares` IS `it increases the number of shares`
            `increase in the par value of shares` IS `it increases the par value of shares`
            `change of shares with par value into shares without par value` IS `it changes shares with par value into shares without par value`
            `change of shares without par value into shares with par value` IS `it changes shares without par value into shares with par value`
        after MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `par shares after the change`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `par value of each after the change, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value after the change`
        before MEANS `s 391 Authorized capital stock` WITH
            `number of authorized shares having par value` IS `par shares before the change`
            `par value of each authorized share having par value, in dollars` IS `par value of each before the change, in dollars`
            `number of authorized shares without par value` IS `shares without par value before the change`

@export What fee does the Secretary of State charge for a service for which section 391 provides no fee, in dollars (s 391(a)(22))?
GIVEN `the fee provided for in section 2315 of Title 29` IS A NUMBER @desc What fee does section 2315 of Title 29 provide for the service, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(a)(22) What fee applies to a service section 391 does not provide for` IS
    `s 391(a)(22) the fee of the Secretary of State for a service for which this section provides no fee` `the fee provided for in section 2315 of Title 29`

§§ `391(c) to (j) - copies, exemption, credit, refunds, returned checks, faster service, good standing`

@export What fee must I pay for photocopies or electronic image copies that the Secretary of State does not certify, in dollars (s 391(c))?
GIVEN `the number of pages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages do you want copied?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(c) What fee must I pay for uncertified copies` IS
    `s 391(c) the fee for photocopies or electronic image copies that the Secretary of State does not certify` `the number of pages`

@export Can I require the Secretary of State to give me public records in a given form (s 391(c))?
GIVEN `the form I ask for is` IS A `s 391(c) Form in which copies of public records are asked for` @desc In what form do you ask for the records: photocopies, electronic image copies, or copies (or access to copies) in an electronic medium or any other form, including bulk data, databases and digital copies?
      `I have paid the fees for each record associated with a file number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid the fees described in section 391, or in section 2318 of Title 29, for each such record associated with a file number?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(c) Can I require the records in the form I ask for` IF
    `s 391(c) the Secretary of State must provide the public records in the form asked for` `the form I ask for is` `I have paid the fees for each record associated with a file number`

@export Is my corporation exempt from fees for the use of the State because it was incorporated for the drainage and reclamation of lowlands (s 391(d))?
GIVEN `my corporation was incorporated for the drainage and reclamation of lowlands` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the corporation incorporated for the drainage and reclamation of lowlands?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(d) Is my corporation exempt from fees for the use of the State` IS
    `s 391(d) no fee for the use of the State is charged or collected from the corporation` `my corporation was incorporated for the drainage and reclamation of lowlands`

@export Can I pay the fees on credit (s 391(e))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has permitted me credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State, in the Secretary of State's discretion, permitted the extension of credit for the fees on terms?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(e) Can I pay the fees on credit` IF
    `s 391(e) the fees may be paid on credit` `the Secretary of State has permitted me credit`

@export How much of what I paid the Secretary of State may be refunded, in dollars (s 391(f))?
GIVEN `what I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you pay the Secretary of State, in dollars?
      `what section 391 required` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did section 391 require, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(f) How much of my payment may be refunded` IS
    `s 391(f) the part of a payment that exceeds the fees required, which the Secretary of State may refund` `what I paid` `what section 391 required`

@export What can I be charged for a check that was returned or stopped, in dollars (s 391(g))?
GIVEN `the check was for a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the check received for payment of a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title?
      `the check was returned for insufficient funds or stopped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it returned due to insufficient funds or as the result of a stop payment order?
      `the Secretary of State charges the fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State, in the Secretary of State's discretion, charge the fee?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(g) What can I be charged for a returned check` IS
    `s 391(g) the charge for a returned check` `the check was for a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6` `the check was returned for insufficient funds or stopped` `the Secretary of State charges the fee`

@export What is the most I can be charged in addition for faster service, in dollars (s 391(h))?
GIVEN `the speed I ask for is` IS A `s 391(h) Speed at which a service is requested` @desc How fast do you ask for the service to be completed?
      `the service is one described in subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service one described in subsection (a) of section 391 (a filing or other service listed there)?
      `the service is one described in subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service one described in subsection (c) of section 391 (copies of instruments and other papers)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 391(h) What is the most I can be charged for faster service` IS
    `s 391(h) the most that may be added to the fees for the service` `the speed I ask for is` `the service is one described in subsection (a)` `the service is one described in subsection (c)`

@export Is the additional sum in the Secretary of State's schedule for faster service within the limit (s 391(h))?
GIVEN `the speed I ask for is` IS A `s 391(h) Speed at which a service is requested` @desc How fast do you ask for the service to be completed?
      `the service is one described in subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service one described in subsection (a) of section 391?
      `the service is one described in subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service one described in subsection (c) of section 391?
      `the additional sum I am charged, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What additional sum are you charged for the faster service, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(h) Is the additional sum I am charged within the limit` IS
    `s 391(h) the additional sum in the schedule is within the limit` `the speed I ask for is` `the service is one described in subsection (a)` `the service is one described in subsection (c)` `the additional sum I am charged, in dollars`

-- s 391(i). Good standing: the corporation's side and the filer's side.
@export Has my corporation ceased to be in good standing (or registered) because it did not pay a fee or tax after a written demand (s 391(i))?
GIVEN `we filed an instrument and failed to pay a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation file an instrument or certificate and neglect, refuse or fail to pay a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or Chapter 6 of this title?
      `the Secretary of State has mailed a written demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State mailed a written demand for it to the corporation in care of its registered agent in Delaware?
      `the date the demand was mailed` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date was the demand mailed? (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-01-01; ignored if none)
      `we have paid the fee or tax in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the fee or tax, and any returned-check fee under subsection (g), been paid in full?
      `the date we paid in full` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (ISO 8601; ignored if not paid)
      `the date I ask about` IS A DATE @desc For which date do you ask? (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(i) Has my corporation ceased to be in good standing for non-payment` IF
    `s 391(i) the corporation has ceased to be in good standing or registered` `we filed an instrument and failed to pay a fee or tax under Chapter 1 or 6`
        (IF `the Secretary of State has mailed a written demand` THEN JUST `the date the demand was mailed` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `we have paid the fee or tax in full` THEN JUST `the date we paid in full` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the date I ask about`

@export Is my corporation restored to good standing once it pays what it owed (s 391(i))?
GIVEN `my corporation has ceased to be in good standing for non-payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation ceased to be in good standing, or a foreign corporation ceased to be registered, by reason of neglect, refusal or failure to pay a fee or tax?
      `we have paid the fee or tax` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the fee or tax that was neglected been paid?
      `a returned-check fee under subsection (g) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the fee provided for in subsection (g) apply?
      `we have paid the returned-check fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it applies, has it been paid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(i) Is my corporation restored to good standing` IF
    `s 391(i) the corporation is restored to good standing or registered status` `my corporation has ceased to be in good standing for non-payment` `we have paid the fee or tax` `a returned-check fee under subsection (g) applies` `we have paid the returned-check fee`

@export Is the Secretary of State barred from accepting my corporation's filings or issuing it a certificate of good standing (s 391(i))?
GIVEN `my corporation has ceased to be in good standing for non-payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation ceased to be in good standing, or a foreign corporation ceased to be registered, by reason of neglect, refusal or failure to pay a fee or tax?
      `my corporation has been restored` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been restored to good standing (or registered status)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 391(i) Is the Secretary of State barred from accepting my filings` IF
    `s 391(i) the Secretary of State is barred from accepting an instrument for filing from the corporation or issuing a certificate of good standing for it` `my corporation has ceased to be in good standing for non-payment` `my corporation has been restored`

§ `Sections 393 to 398 - general provisions`

§§ `393, 394 - earlier laws; the State's reserved power; the chapter as part of my corporation's charter`

@export Does this chapter impair a right, suit or duty that I have under an earlier law (s 393)?
GIVEN `what I have is` IS A `s 393 Kind of thing that an earlier law gave or imposed` @desc What is it: a right, privilege or immunity vested or accrued; a suit pending; a right of action conferred; a duty, restriction, liability or penalty imposed or required; or something else?
      `it arises by and under a law enacted before this chapter was adopted or amended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it arise by and under a law enacted before the adoption or amendment of this chapter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 393 Is my right, suit or duty under an earlier law left unimpaired` IS
    `s 393 this chapter leaves the right, suit or duty under an earlier law unimpaired` `what I have is` `it arises by and under a law enacted before this chapter was adopted or amended`

@export If the General Assembly amends or repeals this chapter, do I keep my remedy against a corporation or its officers for a liability already incurred (s 394)?
GIVEN `the remedy is under this chapter against a corporation or its officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the remedy one under this chapter against a corporation or its officers?
      `the liability was incurred before the amendment or repeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the liability incurred before the amendment or repeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 394 Do I keep my remedy after an amendment or repeal` IS
    `s 394 the remedy survives an amendment or repeal of this chapter` `the remedy is under this chapter against a corporation or its officers` `the liability was incurred before the amendment or repeal`

@export Is a provision of this chapter part of my corporation's charter or certificate of incorporation (s 394)?
GIVEN `the provision is inapplicable to the objects of my corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision inapplicable to the objects of the corporation?
      `the provision is inappropriate to the objects of my corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision inappropriate to the objects of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 394 Is the provision part of my corporation's charter` IF
    `s 394 a provision of this chapter is part of the corporation's charter or certificate of incorporation` `the provision is inapplicable to the objects of my corporation` `the provision is inappropriate to the objects of my corporation`

§§ `395 - the word "trust" in a corporation's name`

@export Does the exception in section 395(d) free my corporation from the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b)?
GIVEN `my corporation is subject to the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation subject to the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner of Delaware?
      `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or section 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 (12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq.) or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act (12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq.)?
      `our use of the word trust clearly does not refer to a trust business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the use of the word "trust" in the name clearly not refer to a trust business?
      `our use of the word trust is clearly not likely to mislead the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use clearly not likely to mislead the public into believing that the corporation's business includes activities supervised by the State Bank Commissioner or regulated under those federal Acts?
      `the Director of the Division of Corporations and the State Bank Commissioner have determined there will be no pattern and practice of abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the Director of the Division of Corporations and the State Bank Commissioner determined that the use will not lead to a pattern and practice of abuse that might cause harm to the interests of the public or the State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 395(d) Does the exception free my corporation` IF
    `s 395(d) the requirements and restrictions of subsections (a) and (b) do not apply to the corporation` `my corporation is subject to the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or section 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` `our use of the word trust clearly does not refer to a trust business` `our use of the word trust is clearly not likely to mislead the public` `the Director of the Division of Corporations and the State Bank Commissioner have determined there will be no pattern and practice of abuse`

@export Is my corporation under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner, and must it make reports to the Commissioner (s 395(a))?
GIVEN `my corporation uses the word trust as part of its name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation use the word "trust" as part of its name?
      `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or section 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 (12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq.) or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act (12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq.)?
      `the exception in section 395(d) applies to my corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the exception in section 395(d) apply to the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 395(a) Is my corporation under the Commissioner's supervision and must it report` IF
    `s 395(a) the corporation is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner and must make reports to the Commissioner` `my corporation uses the word trust as part of its name` `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or section 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` `the exception in section 395(d) applies to my corporation`

@export How many reports must a corporation under the State Bank Commissioner's supervision make each year (s 395(a))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 395(a) How many reports must my corporation make each year` IS
    `s 395(a) the fewest reports that the corporation must make to the Commissioner during each year`

@export How many directors must sign to attest each report to the State Bank Commissioner (s 395(a))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 395(a) How many directors must attest each report` IS
    `s 395(a) the fewest directors whose signatures must attest each report`

@export Is this report to the State Bank Commissioner in the form, verified and attested as section 395(a) requires?
GIVEN `the report is in the form prescribed by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the report according to the form prescribed by the Commissioner?
      `the president or a vice-president verified it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it verified by the oath or affirmation of the president or a vice-president?
      `the treasurer or the secretary verified it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it verified by the oath or affirmation of the treasurer or the secretary of the corporation?
      `the number of directors who signed to attest it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors signed to attest the report?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 395(a) Is my report in the form, verified and attested as required` IF
    `s 395(a) the report is in the form, verified and attested as required` report
    WHERE
        report MEANS `s 395(a) Report made to the State Bank Commissioner` WITH
            `report is in the form prescribed by the Commissioner` IS `the report is in the form prescribed by the Commissioner`
            `report is verified by the oath or affirmation of the president or vice-president` IS `the president or a vice-president verified it`
            `report is verified by the oath or affirmation of the treasurer or secretary` IS `the treasurer or the secretary verified it`
            `directors whose signatures attest the report` IS `the number of directors who signed to attest it`

@export Has my corporation made enough reports to the State Bank Commissioner this year (s 395(a))?
GIVEN `the number of reports this year that are in the form, verified and attested` IS A NUMBER @desc How many reports have been made this year that are in the prescribed form, verified as required and attested by at least 3 directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 395(a) Has my corporation made enough reports this year` IF
    `s 395(a) the corporation has made enough reports during the year` `the number of reports this year that are in the form, verified and attested`

@export May my corporation use the word "trust" as part of its name (s 395(b))?
GIVEN `my corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation report to, and is it under the supervision of, the State Bank Commissioner of Delaware?
      `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or section 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 (12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq.) or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act (12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq.)?
      `the exception in section 395(d) applies to my corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the exception in section 395(d) apply to the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 395(b) May my corporation use the word trust in its name` IF
    `s 395(b) the corporation may use the word trust as part of its name` `my corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or section 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` `the exception in section 395(d) applies to my corporation`

@export May my corporation amend its name to include the word "trust" (s 395(b))?
GIVEN `my corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation report to, and is it under the supervision of, the State Bank Commissioner of Delaware?
      `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or the Savings and Loan Holding Company Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or the Savings and Loan Holding Company Act?
      `the exception in section 395(d) applies to my corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the exception in section 395(d) apply to the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 395(b) May my corporation amend its name to include trust` IF
    `s 395(b) the corporation's name may be amended so as to include the word trust` `my corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or the Savings and Loan Holding Company Act` `the exception in section 395(d) applies to my corporation`

@export May my corporation advertise or put forth a sign as a trust company, or solicit or receive deposits or transact business as one (s 395(c))?
GIVEN `my corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation report to, and is it under the supervision of, the State Bank Commissioner of Delaware?
      `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or section 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 (12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq.) or § 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act (12 U.S.C. § 1467a et seq.)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 395(c) May my corporation act as a trust company` IF
    `s 395(c) the corporation may advertise, solicit or receive deposits or transact business as a trust company` `my corporation reports to and is under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner` `my corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act or section 10 of the Home Owners' Loan Act`

§§ `396 to 398 - copies of the chapter; the penalty for publishing it; its name`

@export May the Secretary of State charge me this sum for a pamphlet copy of this chapter (s 396)?
GIVEN `the sum I am charged for the copy, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum are you charged for a pamphlet copy of this chapter, in dollars?
      `the cost of printing that copy, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the cost of printing that copy, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 396 May the Secretary of State charge me this sum for a pamphlet copy` IS
    `s 396 the sum charged for a pamphlet copy is within the limit` `the sum I am charged for the copy, in dollars` `the cost of printing that copy, in dollars`

@export May the Secretary of State give out a single pamphlet copy of this chapter free (s 396)?
GIVEN `the number of copies given free to one person` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pamphlet copies of this chapter are given out free to one person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 396 May the Secretary of State give out a pamphlet copy free` IS
    `s 396 this section does not prevent the free distribution` `the number of copies given free to one person`

@export Do I commit the offence in section 397 if I print or publish this chapter (s 397)?
GIVEN `I print or publish this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you print or publish this chapter?
      `I have the authority of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the authority of the Secretary of State of Delaware to print or publish it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 397 Do I commit the offence by printing or publishing this chapter` IF
    `s 397 the person has printed or published this chapter without authority` `I print or publish this chapter` `I have the authority of the Secretary of State`

@export What is the most I can be fined for printing or publishing this chapter without authority, in dollars (s 397)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 397 What is the most I can be fined` IS
    `s 397 the greatest fine for printing or publishing this chapter without authority`

@export What is the longest term of imprisonment, in months, for printing or publishing this chapter without authority (s 397)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 397 What is the longest term of imprisonment` IS
    `s 397 the greatest term of imprisonment, in months, for printing or publishing this chapter without authority`

@export Is a fine and term of imprisonment within the limits of section 397 (s 397)?
GIVEN `the person printed or published this chapter without authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person print or publish this chapter without the authority of the Secretary of State?
      `the fine, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What fine is in question, in dollars?
      `the term of imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc What term of imprisonment is in question, in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 397 Is the penalty within the limits` IS
    `s 397 the penalty is within the limits` `the person printed or published this chapter without authority` `the fine, in dollars` `the term of imprisonment, in months`

@export What is the short title of this chapter (s 398)?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `s 398 What is the short title of this chapter` IS
    `s 398 the short title of the chapter`

@export May I refer to this chapter by this name (s 398)?
GIVEN `the name` IS A STRING @desc What name do you use for the chapter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 398 May I refer to this chapter by this name` IS
    `s 398 the name may be used to refer to the chapter` `the name`
